\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. All things praise Thee, Lord most high
\par Heaven and earth and sea and sky,
\par All were for Thy glory made,
\par That Thy greatness thus displayed
\par Should all worship brings to Thee;
\par All things praise Thee; Lord, may we.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. All things praise Thee ; night to night,
\par Sings in silent hymns of light;
\par All things praise Thee; day to day
\par Chants thy power, in burning ray;
\par Time and space are praising Thee
\par All things praise Thee; Lord may we.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. All things praise Thee round her zones
\par Earth, with her ten thousand tones
\par Rolls a ceaseless choral strain;
\par Roaring wind and deep-voiced main,
\par Rustling leaf and humming bee,
\par All things praise Thee; Lord may we.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. All things praise Thee; high and low
\par Rain and dew and seven-hued bow,
\par Crimson sunset, fleecy cloud
\par Rippling stream and tempest loud;
\par Summer, winter, all to Thee;
\par Glory render; Lord may we.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. All things praise Thee; gracious Lord,
\par Great Creator, powerful word
\par Omnipresent Spirit, now
\par At Thy feet we humbly bow
\par Lift our hearts in praise to Thee;
\par All things praise Thee ; Lord may we.
\par                                             Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

